WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.303
"Ow—drat!" Zann said as he landed in a clawthorn bush.

2
00:00:07.304 --> 00:00:11.481
"That's what you get for zapping in a hurry," Perda said with a laugh.

3
00:00:11.482 --> 00:00:19.413
Zann pushed the prickly branches aside. He frowned when he saw that Perda wasn't alone. Darb and Gliss were with her.

4
00:00:19.414 --> 00:00:26.098
"Hi, Zann," Gliss said as Zann climbed out of the bush. "Need help healing those scratches?"

5
00:00:26.099 --> 00:00:29.795
"No, thanks." Zann wasn't ready to forgive Gliss yet.

6
00:00:29.796 --> 00:00:36.830
If she hadn't ratted him out to Boz, he might be searching for his parents right now instead of being stuck in Swamp Bottom!

7
00:00:36.831 --> 00:00:44.240
"Um, okay." Gliss sounded tentative. "Listen, Zann. Can we talk for a second? I really want to—"

8
00:00:44.241 --> 00:00:51.529
"Not now," Zann interrupted. "Perda's note sounded urgent." He turned toward Perda. "What's up?"

9
00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:57.769
"I ran into Professor Huli this morning," Perda said. "I asked her about World X."

10
00:00:57.770 --> 00:01:01.320
Professor Huli was the kids' Advanced Magic teacher.

11
00:01:01.321 --> 00:01:05.135
If anyone might know about World X, it was she.

12
00:01:05.136 --> 00:01:09.013
"Really?" Zann said eagerly. "What did she say?"

13
00:01:09.014 --> 00:01:12.305
Perda shrugged. "She's never heard of it."

14
00:01:12.306 --> 00:01:20.726
Zann's heart sank. "Oh well. My parents' message made it sound like World X might be a newly discovered world.

15
00:01:20.727 --> 00:01:27.292
So it's no surprise if most people—even an Advanced Magic teacher—haven't heard of it."

16
00:01:27.293 --> 00:01:32.963
"I don't understand," Darb said. "How is it possible World X was just discovered?

17
00:01:32.964 --> 00:01:36.139
I thought people have been everywhere through the vortex."

18
00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:42.871
"No, definitely not," Perda said. "There are probably lots of worlds that haven't been discovered yet.

19
00:01:42.872 --> 00:01:46.325
Most worlds are actually really difficult to find.

20
00:01:46.326 --> 00:01:57.095
There isn't always a direct route from one place to another, and wormholes open and close all the time, which makes travel through them even more complicated."

21
00:01:57.096 --> 00:02:01.191
Gliss nodded. "We just learned about all that in school."

22
00:02:01.192 --> 00:02:07.709
"So if Zann's parents got knocked off course by that weird otherworld animal—" Darb glanced at Zann.

23
00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:12.941
"A scatter beast," Zann said. "They're from a world called Fardark.

24
00:02:12.942 --> 00:02:18.448
My parents mentioned them in one of their books, but nobody knows much about them."

25
00:02:18.449 --> 00:02:22.290
"Zann's parents could be anywhere," Perda continued.

26
00:02:22.291 --> 00:02:25.987
"For all we know, they're in World X right now!"

27
00:02:25.988 --> 00:02:31.915
"Or maybe they're asking around about it while they're looking for a way back to Magica," Zann said.

28
00:02:31.916 --> 00:02:37.102
"It might be a clue, anyway. If I can get myself back into the vortex—"

29
00:02:37.103 --> 00:02:44.001
"That reminds me," Perda interrupted. "You never told us about your trip with Wyssa. What was it like?"

30
00:02:44.002 --> 00:02:48.573
"Well, I wasn't in the vortex for long . . ." Zann began.

31
00:02:48.574 --> 00:02:53.112
It was hard to describe the experience. But he did his best.

32
00:02:53.113 --> 00:02:57.232
"Wow. I bet it was cool!" Perda looked impressed.

33
00:02:57.233 --> 00:03:00.183
"But it sounds like Wyssa did all the work.

34
00:03:00.184 --> 00:03:03.761
Do you think you could navigate through the vortex on your own?"

35
00:03:03.762 --> 00:03:06.915
Zann shrugged. "I'll figure it out."

36
00:03:06.916 --> 00:03:12.028
"What if you don't have enough magic?" Darb sounded worried. "You're only a kid." "I'm

37
00:03:12.029 --> 00:03:17.499
a Red too." Zann touched his hair, trying to sound confident. "That

38
00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:20.139
should give me some extra power." "It

39
00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:24.227
just sounds too dangerous, Zann," Gliss said. Zann

40
00:03:24.228 --> 00:03:29.708
frowned. " Everything sounds too dangerous to you," he snapped.

41
00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:34.017
"Especially when it's my parents who are missing instead of yours!"

42
00:03:34.018 --> 00:03:41.020
Gliss gasped, and tears came to her eyes. "I—I have to go," she mumbled.

43
00:03:41.021 --> 00:03:43.994
Snapping her fingers, she zapped out of sight.

44
00:03:43.995 --> 00:03:47.911
"Zann!" Perda scowled at him. "That was mean!"

45
00:03:47.912 --> 00:03:52.431
"Gliss was just worried about you," Darb added. He glanced at Perda.

46
00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:54.647
"Will you take me to check on her?"

47
00:03:54.648 --> 00:03:58.232
"Sure." Perda grabbed Darb's hand. "Zap!"

48
00:03:58.233 --> 00:04:01.751
They disappeared, leaving Zann alone with Zing.

49
00:04:01.752 --> 00:04:04.986
Zann felt guilty for hurting Gliss' feelings.

50
00:04:04.987 --> 00:04:07.745
But he did his best to shake off his guilt.

51
00:04:07.746 --> 00:04:10.820
In a few days he would be stuck at school.

52
00:04:10.821 --> 00:04:14.998
This could be his last chance to come up with a plan to find his parents.

53
00:04:14.999 --> 00:04:19.578
If his friends didn't want to help, he would do it on his own.

54
00:04:19.579 --> 00:04:22.968
Two days later Zann was no closer to a plan.

55
00:04:22.969 --> 00:04:30.277
He'd researched the locations of all the known wormholes in Magica, but they were all far away from Swamp Bottom.

56
00:04:30.278 --> 00:04:38.979
Zapping to any of those wormholes would use up all his energy, leaving little or no energy to navigate through the vortex.

57
00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:41.993
He would have to rest for at least a day first.

58
00:04:41.994 --> 00:04:49.783
That would give Boz enough time to notice Zann was missing, figure out what was going on, and stop Zann from leaving Magica.

59
00:04:49.784 --> 00:04:54.945
The day before school was due to start, Zann zapped to the swamp to meet Darb.

60
00:04:54.946 --> 00:04:58.673
Darb had stopped by earlier to set up a time and place to meet.

61
00:04:58.674 --> 00:05:02.493
But when Zann reached their meeting spot, nobody was there.

62
00:05:02.494 --> 00:05:08.525
That was surprising. Darb was almost always on time. Zann sat down to wait.

63
00:05:08.526 --> 00:05:13.788
A moment later Gliss zapped into view. "Hi, Zann," she said.

64
00:05:13.789 --> 00:05:18.016
Zann jumped to his feet. "What are you doing here?"

65
00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:22.790
"I asked Darb to arrange to meet you so I could talk to you alone," Gliss said.

66
00:05:22.791 --> 00:05:27.905
"You mean you asked him to help you trick me." Zann frowned.

67
00:05:27.906 --> 00:05:33.409
"I'm sorry!" Gliss exclaimed. "But I've been trying to apologize, and you won't—"

68
00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:40.177
Suddenly Perda zapped into view. "Zann!" she cried, her eyes wide and excited.

69
00:05:40.178 --> 00:05:44.947
"I've been looking for you! I need to talk to you—now!"

70
00:05:44.948 --> 00:05:55.804
"No problem," said Zann before Perda had a chance to notice Gliss standing behind her. Grabbing Perda's hand, he said, "Zap!"

71
00:05:55.805 --> 00:05:57.893
They landed in another part of the swamp.

72
00:05:57.894 --> 00:06:01.954
Perda looked confused. "Why did you zap us away?"

73
00:06:01.955 --> 00:06:06.274
"Never mind," Zann said. "What did you want to talk about?"

74
00:06:06.275 --> 00:06:13.244
"Oh!" Perda smiled. "Right. Listen to this—I just found a new wormhole.

75
00:06:13.245 --> 00:06:19.413
And it's right here in Swamp Bottom!"

